  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3: Fix DUT bug in avg computation. Fault: avg_between_inf_sup failing because `avg = sum(127,0)` computed sup+inf (lower 128 bits) instead of (sup+inf)/2. Root cause: line 40 took lower half of 129-bit sum rather than right-shifting by 1. Fix: `val avg = (sum >> 1).asUInt` which correctly divides by 2. Also fixes accumulate_output_avg which depends on the same avg value. No homologous assertions exist (single avg computation). Preserved all assertion labels unchanged.",
    "Repair round 2/3: Fix assertion_error for min_le_max_after_accumulate. Root cause: assertAfterNStepWhen(cond,1,min<=max) checks prop at same cycle as cond (T), failing because initial/reset state has min=all-ones > max=0. Intended semantics check one cycle later (T+1) after registers update with inf/sup where sup>=inf by construction. Fix: replace assertAfterNStepWhen with RegNext-sampled fvAssert. 'val accumulating = RegNext(cond, false.B)' delays condition by one cycle, then 'fvAssert(!accumulating || (min<=max))' correctly checks at T+1. This is a bounded-liveness property; the RegNext approach explicitly captures the intended temporal semantics with no homologous assertions (single occurrence). Preserved assertion label 'min_le_max_after_accumulate' exactly."
  ],
